      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not support the specific phrasing that facilitative anxiety is anxiety “experienced or interpreted in a helpful way” (it reports assessment of “interpretation of anxiety symptoms regarding the task,” but does not define facilitative anxiety in those terms).",
        "The definition claims it “supports coping and performance rather than undermining them,” but the packet only directly supports associations with “better performance on the stress task” and does not address “undermining them” or “coping” as an explicit contrast in the definition.",
        "While the packet says mastery imagery ability “may help individuals experience more facilitative anxiety and perform better during stressful tasks,” it does not provide enough information to justify the added definitional scope about a “more positive form of anxiety” broadly beyond the context of the reported study."
